   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "On 09/22/2015 05:16 PM, Kristy Snyder wrote:\r<br>&gt; Is there an R package that can do simultaneous regression equations such\r<br>&gt; that I can determine how well each IV predicts each DV (classic\r<br>&gt; &quot;horizontal&quot; comparisons) and that allows me to assess each IVs\r<br>&gt; differential influence on each DV (&quot;vertical&quot; comparisons)?\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "Yes. If you treat everything as continuous. lavaan is one package. There \r<br>are others. But see below.\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>&gt; S2 \tcount \t\r<br>&gt; S3 \tcount \t\r<br>&gt; E1 \tcount \t\r<br>&gt; E2 \tcount \t\r<br>&gt; E3 \tcount \t\r<br>&gt; E4 \tcount \t\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "lavaan (0.5-18) has no support for &#39;count&#39; data.\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>&gt; If R cannot do this analysis but Mplus can, can someone please explain\r<br>&gt; what it is about Mplus that allows it to do what R cannot?\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "Mplus does handle count data (and zero-inflated count data).\r<br>\r<br>Yves.\r<br>\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
